Job Description
Maintain liaison between the factory management with STA Technical Training Department.
Observe implementing the technical training program at the factory.
Eliminate inconsistencies in quality, health and safety during the practical training process.
Follow up on the attendance and departure of students during entry and exit from the factory.
Follow the safety and security laws, starting with the student leaving the academy, getting on and off the car inside the factory and also ensure all student wears all his safety and security clothing.
Ensure that students are distributed in the departments concerned with their training and are present in the place designated for them on the specified dates.
Ensure that each student has a report brochure and a training plan.
Follow-up students during the day to ensure their commitment to the place of training and follow-up instructions for safety, safety and occupational health.
Ensure that the student is not in unsafe places during the training period or that he performs unauthorized dangerous work.
Prepare a daily and monthly report to be presented to the Senior Technical Trainer.
Evaluate students’ progress on a regular basis, including progress reports and quarterly grades.
Job Requirements
Bachelor’s degree in computer engineering or information technology or computer science.&nbsp;
Java SE.&nbsp;
Java Object Oriented Programming.&nbsp;
JDBC.&nbsp;
At least one desktop Application.&nbsp;
Problem Solving.&nbsp;
Oracle SQL &amp; PL/ SQL (is plus).&nbsp;
&nbsp;Web Development knowledge (is preferred).&nbsp;
We will provide:
&nbsp;Three-month training after acceptation.&nbsp;
&nbsp;Oracle Certified (Java Foundation) after the training period.&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Job Description
Own and deliver solutions within the scope of the role, from requirements and technical/design decisions through implementation and continuous improvement.&nbsp;
Work closely with engineering, product, data, design, and business stakeholders to translate requirements into practical, scalable solutions.&nbsp;
Apply strong engineering and/or domain expertise to build reliable, maintainable, and production-ready capabilities.&nbsp;
Contribute to architecture, standards, documentation, quality, and technical decision-making appropriate to the role.&nbsp;
Identify performance, scalability, data quality, usability, reliability, or operational risks and address them proactively.&nbsp;
Collaborate across teams to ensure solutions integrate effectively with existing systems and platform components.&nbsp;
Job Requirements
Experience: 7+ years of relevant professional experience.&nbsp;
Strong hands-on experience with: Telco data modelling, TM Forum SID, BSS and OSS data, CDR and xDR, identity resolution, SQL, data mapping.&nbsp;
Strong working knowledge of TM Forum SID, eTOM, and 3GPP charging and CDR structures.&nbsp;
Practical understanding of BSS and OSS: product catalog, order, mediation, rating, billing, collections, inventory.&nbsp;
Clear grasp of party, customer, account, subscriber, and service, and why flattening them breaks B2B and family plans.&nbsp;
Has worked on identity resolution using MSISDN, including portability, SIM swap, and number recycling.&nbsp;
Maps source systems to a canonical model and writes implementable specifications, not slide decks.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Domain Requirement:&nbsp;
Telco is a must&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Preferred Qualifications&nbsp;
Customer data platform or single customer view delivery.&nbsp;
Consent and data governance frameworks.&nbsp;
Experience running requirements workshops with client stakeholders.&nbsp;

Job Description
We are currently seeking a skilled and experienced Data Scientist to join our team. As a Data Scientist, you will be responsible for experiments with datasets searching for useful insights and features, maintaining data pipelines and training machine learning algorithms, and visualizing results.
&nbsp;
Main goals and responsibilities:
Be a proactive team worker;
Collaborate with the team to implement new features to support the growing data needs;
Build, maintain, and deploy DS and ML pipelines, including data retrieval, preprocessing, feature engineering, training, and inferencing the models, analyzing and visualizing the results;
Build, maintain and deploy LLM-powered systems and agent pipelines, including prompt engineering, tool and API integration, memory and context management, inference orchestration, and evaluation of model outputs;
Share knowledge with other teams on various data science or project-related topics;
Collaborate with the team to decide on which tools and strategies to use within specific scenarios.
&nbsp;
What We Offer:
Long-term career stability with a competitive salary paid in USD.
Conditions for steady career development.
Development supported by dedicated mentors and a variety of programs focused on expertise and innovation.
Private medical insurance provided after successful completion of the probationary period
A well-equipped and cozy office supports comfort and productivity across all project stages.
Welcoming atmosphere and a friendly corporate culture.
Job Requirements
Required:
English level upper intermediate+;
Good mathematical and statistical background, tensor calculus;
Good knowledge of databases such as Postgres, MongoDB, and SQL;
Python language including practical experience with Scikit-learn, Numpy, Pandas, and Matplot libraries;
Experience with gradient boosting algorithms (XGBoost or LightGBM);
Familiarity with LLM orchestration tools (e.g., LangChain, LangGraph);
Experience using or integrating with cloud LLM APIs (e.g., OpenAI, Claude, Amazon Bedrock, Vertex AI);
Hands-on experience with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines and vector databases (e.g., pgvector, FAISS, Weaviate, Pinecone);
Practical experience with prompt engineering techniques, agentic tools and workflows;
At least 1 framework to build and train neural networks (TensorFlow/Keras, PyTorch), a good understanding of neural networks architectures, and how-tos;
Commercial experience with classic machine learning and deep learning, including NLP and CV models like Bert, Resnet;
Practical skills in building en-to-end ML training pipelines (data load, preprocess, train, inference), as well as GitHub / GitLab CI/CD flows;
Docker or Kubernetes platform;
Work experience as a Data Scientist more than 2 years.
Nice to have:
Hands-on experience with at least one major cloud platform (AWS, Azure, or GCP);
Ability to work with Spark, Airflow.

Job Description
We are looking for an experienced Senior Product Designer who combines strong visual design skills with a deep understanding of user experience, product thinking, and business objectives.&nbsp;
You will lead the end-to-end design process across multiple product areas, from discovery and research through wireframing, prototyping, testing, and final implementation. You'll be responsible for creating intuitive, scalable, and elegant experiences while helping establish and evolve our design systems and product design standards.&nbsp;
Job Requirements
5+ years of experience in Product Design, UX/UI Design, or a related field&nbsp;
Strong portfolio demonstrating end-to-end product design work across web and mobile applications&nbsp;
Expertise in user-centered design methodologies and design thinking principles&nbsp;
Advanced proficiency in Figma and modern design tools&nbsp;
Experience creating and maintaining design systems&nbsp;
Strong understanding of information architecture, interaction design, and visual design principles&nbsp;
Experience working closely with software engineering teams and understanding technical constraints&nbsp;
Ability to balance user needs, business goals, and technical feasibility&nbsp;
Excellent communication, storytelling, and stakeholder management skills&nbsp;
Strong problem-solving and analytical thinking abilities&nbsp;
Comfortable working in fast-paced startup environments with evolving priorities

Job Description
Department&nbsp;: Digital Manufacturing Solutions&nbsp;
Job Summary&nbsp;
The Digital Manufacturing Consultant is responsible for implementing, configuring, and supporting Siemens Digital Industries Software solutions, primarily Teamcenter and Opcenter, to enable customers' digital manufacturing transformation. The role works closely with engineering, production, quality, and IT teams to analyze manufacturing processes, design digital solutions, lead implementation activities, and ensure successful project delivery.&nbsp;
Key Responsibilities&nbsp;
Manufacturing Consulting&nbsp;
Analyze manufacturing and engineering business processes.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Conduct customer workshops and process assessments.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Identify digital transformation opportunities.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Recommend industry best practices.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Prepare functional solution designs.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Teamcenter Implementation&nbsp;
Configure Teamcenter according to customer requirements.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Support data migration and system integration.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Configure workflows and business rules.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Conduct functional testing and validation.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Support production deployment and Go-Live.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Opcenter (MES) Consulting&nbsp;
Implement Siemens Opcenter solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Configure manufacturing execution processes.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Support production scheduling and execution.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Integrate shop-floor equipment where applicable.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Optimize manufacturing workflows.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Customer Engagement&nbsp;
Act as the primary functional consultant.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Facilitate design workshops.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Prepare customer documentation.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Deliver administrator and end-user training.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Provide post-Go-Live support.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Continuous Improvement&nbsp;
Recommend process optimization opportunities.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Identify additional solution opportunities.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Maintain implementation standards.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Share lessons learned with the consulting team.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Job Requirements
Qualifications&nbsp;
Bachelor's Degree in Automation Engineering,, Industrial Engineering, Computer Engineering, or equivalent.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Around one year of experience implementing manufacturing software solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Technical Skills&nbsp;
Siemens Solutions&nbsp;
Siemens Teamcenter&nbsp;&nbsp;
Siemens Opcenter MES&nbsp;&nbsp;
Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES)&nbsp;&nbsp;
Product Lifecycle Management (PLM)&nbsp;&nbsp;
Manufacturing Knowledge&nbsp;
Manufacturing Operations&nbsp;&nbsp;
Production Planning&nbsp;&nbsp;
Shop Floor Processes&nbsp;&nbsp;
Quality Management&nbsp;&nbsp;
Manufacturing KPIs&nbsp;&nbsp;
Technical Skills&nbsp;
Fundamental Computer networking&nbsp;&nbsp;
C# .Net, SQL&nbsp;&nbsp;
Fundamental PLC programming&nbsp;&nbsp;
REST APIs (preferred)&nbsp;&nbsp;
Soft Skills&nbsp;
Customer Consulting&nbsp;&nbsp;
Business Process Analysis&nbsp;&nbsp;
Communication&nbsp;&nbsp;
Workshop Facilitation&nbsp;&nbsp;
Presentation Skills&nbsp;&nbsp;
Problem Solving&nbsp;&nbsp;
Teamwork&nbsp;

Job Description
We are looking for this position someone with an analytical mindset to join our team to work in a friendly analytics department. Here you can participate in finding insights, researching and processing large amounts of data, interacting with end-users, the business analysis of new requests, as well as demonstrating your leadership skills.
Essential Duties and Responsibilities
Identify and define business needs and goals;
Design data models for the entity and pair relationship;
Interact with customer, product, and engineering teams;
Explore, analyze and process massive amounts of data, turning it into actionable business insights;
Applying business analysis and product analytics technics and approaches;
Specification of the requirements;
Build automated dashboards and reports to facilitate company-wide awareness and understanding of key metrics using different BI and analytical tools;
Perform ad hoc analytic requests to transform data into information.
What We Offer
Stable long-term cooperation and competitive compensation.
A fast and well-structured onboarding process with a dedicated mentor.
A clear career development path and access to learning programs.
Paid vacation, national public holidays, and support during religious celebrations.
A modern and comfortable office based in Smart Village, at the heart of Cairo’s tech ecosystem.
Healthy work–life balance.
A welcoming corporate culture, team support, and respectful communication.
Job Requirements
Qualifications
Master’s degree in Economics, Mathematics, Computer science, or similar;
Upper-Intermediate level of English.
Desired Skills
Experience with BI tools (Power BI, Tableau, etc.);
Experience with DBMS (PostgreSQL or others);
Experience with DWH (Snowflake, BigQuery, AWS RedShift, etc.);
Full proficiency in SQL (data modeling, queries, analytic/window functions);
Familiarity with data warehouse and ETL pipelines principles;
Advanced level of MS Excel;
Data mining and data analysis techniques;
Experience in translating business needs/requirements into technical specifications (gathering, presenting, estimating, prioritizing, etc.));
A clear understanding of the principles and specifics of software development methodologies (SDLC);
Extensive knowledge of business analysis techniques (Use case scenarios, User stories, User story mapping, Prioritization techniques, Estimation approaches, etc.)
Communication and negotiation skills to establish and maintain good working relationships with external organizations and internal customers;
Excellent time-management skills, ability to learn quickly and handle multi-tasking activities;
Git/VCS experience.

